-- title:
--   Logarithmic bound for prime powers with a common base
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a number field with ring of integers $\mathcal O_K$, and write $N(I)=|\mathcal O_K/I|$ for the norm of a nonzero integral ideal. Let $P$ be a nonzero prime ideal, $x\ge1$, and $F$ a finite set of distinct prime-power ideals, all of the form $P^e$ with $e\ge1$ and $N(P)^e\le x$. Then
--
--   $$
--   |F|\log N(P)\le\log x.
--   $$
--
--   This bounds the total logarithmic contribution of all selected powers of one prime.
--
--   Source and proof credit: the Tau Ceti contributors, [original declaration and proof](https://github.com/TauCetiProject/TauCeti/blob/948fe4751b1fe528b6d580c522ca5d743d47f185/TauCeti/NumberTheory/ArithmeticDirichletSeries/Counting.lean#L743-L777), Apache-2.0, commit `948fe4751b1fe528b6d580c522ca5d743d47f185`; adapted to Lean 4.33.1.
